    q: "What is temperature and sampling in LLMs?",
    level: 'Advanced',
    a: "Temperature controls how random the next-token choice is: the model's scores are divided by the temperature before softmax. Low temperature (like 0.2) makes the top token dominate, giving focused, repeatable answers, which I use for facts and code. High temperature (like 1.5) flattens the probabilities for more creative output. Top-k and top-p sampling further limit choices to the most likely tokens.",
